{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EPH",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be ye therefore followers of God, as dear children;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And walk in love, as Christ also hath loved us, and hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweet-smelling savor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But lewdness and all uncleanness or covetousness, let it not be once named among you, as becometh saints;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither filthiness, nor foolish talking, nor jesting, which are not convenient: but rather giving of thanks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this ye know, that no lewd, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let no man deceive you with vain words: for because of these things cometh the wrath of God upon the children of disobedience.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be ye not therefore partakers with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye were sometime darkness, but now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " light in the Lord: walk as children of light;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For the fruit of the Spirit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in all goodness, and righteousness, and truth;)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Proving what is acceptable to the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is a shame even to speak of those things which are done by them in secret.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But all things that are reproved, are made manifest by the light: for whatever doth make manifest is light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore he saith, Awake, thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ will give thee light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "See then that ye walk circumspectly, not as fools, but as wise,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Redeeming the time, because the days are evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore be ye not unwise, but understanding what the will of the Lord ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And be not drunk with wine, in which is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Speaking to yourselves in psalms, and hymns, and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Giving thanks always for all things to God and the Father, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wives, submit yourselves to your own husbands, as to the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the husband is the head of the wife, even as Christ is the head of the church: and he is the Savior of the body.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore as the church is subject to Christ, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wives ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to their own husbands in every thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That he might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So ought men to love their wives, as their own bodies. He that loveth his wife, loveth himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For no man ever yet hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as the Lord the church:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are members of his body, of his flesh, and of his bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall be joined to his wife, and they two shall be one flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This is a great mystery: but I speak concerning Christ and the church.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.5.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.5.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, let every one of you in particular so love his wife even as himself: and the wife ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "see",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that she reverence ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " husband.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
